summary:
- topic: Robotics Team Achievement
  text: The South Portland High School robotics team, Riot Crew (Team 58), was recognized
    for their outstanding performance, placing in the top 3% globally at the world
    championships in Houston. Students demonstrated their robot and shared insights
    into their design and competition experience, receiving commendation from the
    Board.
- topic: FY2024 Financial Audit Findings
  text: The Board received a comprehensive report on the FY24 audit, which highlighted
    material weaknesses in grant reconciliation, payroll accrual, and employee benefit
    withholdings, alongside compliance issues related to overspending. The administration
    detailed corrective actions, including a budget freeze and enhanced reconciliation
    procedures, and committed to a follow-up report in six months.
- topic: High School Performance Update
  text: The SOUTH PORTLAND HIGH SCHOOL Principal presented positive data, noting a
    3% reduction in chronic absenteeism, a significant decrease in out-of-school suspensions,
    and improved SAT scores. The school is actively implementing a PBIS framework
    and utilizing pre/post assessment strategies to foster academic growth and positive
    behavior.
- topic: Personnel Decisions and Public Concern
  text: The consent agenda included numerous personnel elections and several resignations
    and retirements, notably the long-serving SOUTH PORTLAND HIGH SCHOOL band director,
    Craig Uffington. A significant portion of public comment was dedicated to expressing
    strong support for two pre-K educators whose contracts were not renewed, raising
    concerns about the district's decision-making and support for staff.
- topic: Policy and Job Description Approvals
  text: The Board approved the second reading of the Superintendent's job description
    and new job descriptions for a Human Resources Manager, a SOUTH PORTLAND HIGH
    SCHOOL Assistant Principal of Teaching and Learning, and a SOUTH PORTLAND HIGH
    SCHOOL Dean of Students. These approvals are part of ongoing district reorganization
    efforts, while a policy on concussion and head injuries was postponed for further
    review.
- topic: Board Communications and Future Initiatives
  text: Board members acknowledged the contributions of outgoing student representative
    Eliot Wertheimer and encouraged participation in upcoming district surveys. Discussions
    also included requests for DEI training for the Board, a workshop to refine the
    budget process, and exploring the possibility of a unified robotics team.
